=3D"qHWMBI0q" target=3D"_blank">prediction</a> =E2=80=94 that US holiday sh=
opping will exceed $1T for the first time ever in 2025 =E2=80=94 came true.=
 NRF estimated that shoppers dropped an average of ~$890 per person on gift=
s, food, and decor, the second-highest since NRF began tracking 23 years ag=
o. <br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Granted, the price of nearly everything has g=
one up, but it was still an odd year for people to spend big. Yet retailers=
 rolled out sales earlier and did what they could to keep prices low, and w=
hile shoppers hunted for bargains and switched to cheaper brands, they stil=
l prioritized spending on gifts. After all, people need some joy in their l=
ives. <br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Economists are feeling mid, as the kids say, =
about US economic growth going into 2026, but do expect inflation to ease g=
radually while still remaining over the Fed=E2=80=99s 2% goal, <a href=3D"h=
ttps://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVKVS126hVLSW6qyDNz7kr3hvV=
_gMC15HQf4qM_h9qg2-ZW0W8wLKSR6lZ3kXW4Yj-kH6kQptWW2wn6Zk2jXlK8N7FsRrMrhBXKW6=
