>Artemis II</a> is the second of NASA=E2=80=99s Artemis missions, intended =
to build a long-term presence on the moon. Scheduled to launch in early 202=
6, Artemis II will be the first crewed flight test of NASA=E2=80=99s Space =
Launch System (SLS) rocket and Orion spacecraft around the moon, marking th=
e first time humans have traveled to the moon since 1972. Humans won=E2=80=
=99t actually set foot on the moon again until Artemis III, scheduled for s=
ome time in 2027.&nbsp;</p>
